Author: Nick Hung <nick@andestech.com>
Date:   Wed Jul 8 23:04:52 2026 +0800

    feat(hybrid): L2C MMIO transport -- Control register (ABI v5), minimal

    Advance the include/ pin to ABI v5, which appends struct hybrid_l2c (the
    L2 cache controller's MMIO register window) after the M-ext block. This
    is the minimal step of the L2C transport: gated on HYBRID_FLAG_L2C, the
    QEMU plugin drains only the boot-static L2C Control Register (physical
    0xE0500000 + 0x0008) via qemu_plugin_read_memory_hwaddr and sets the
    flag whenever the region reads back. The state_diff verify adds one
    l2c.ctrl row that masks the read-only INITSTATUS[14] status bit so a real
    L2C model (which drives it) and QEMU's RAM stub (which does not) compare
    equal. The l2c_drain.S fixture writes 0xA5 to the Control Register and
    hits the ROI marker; test_plugin_l2c_drain.sh asserts the plugin captured
    it. The full-window drain and reset-default test follow in the completion
    step.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

